-- #3728 with #3726: an UNANNOTATED receiver whose only candidate type is `V`.  The
-- two owner keys `R` and `W` are constructors of that one type, so they are one
-- candidate, and the selection then meets the same field-position check an
-- annotated `V` receiver does: `x` sits at a different slot in each constructor, a
-- `V` value carries no constructor tag, and the access is rejected where it is
-- written.
import m.{V, mkW}

g v = v.x

main = putStrLn (intToString (g mkW))
